#!/bin/sh
# Makes build.nbt from scratch: every part in plan order into a temp file, then moved into place.
# The roofs are built inside the parts (parts/roofs.mjs, via vocab.roofPiece), so there is no separate roof step.
set -eu
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
tmpdir="$(mktemp -d)"
trap 'rm -rf "$tmpdir"' EXIT
node build.mjs "$tmpdir/build.nbt"
mv "$tmpdir/build.nbt" build.nbt
echo "build.nbt written"
BUILD: mcmansion-sonnet-high: a suburban McMansion, two storeys plus attic, on a cul-de-sac lot. Recognisable elements: a jumble of roof forms (a tall front gable over the entry, hipped wings, a turret-ish bay, dormers) in dark asphalt shingle; a double-height entry with a two-storey portico, columns and a fanlight window over the door; a mix of facade materials (stone veneer on the lower front, beige siding elsewhere, white trim and quoins); a three-car garage wing with carriage-style doors facing the street; tall arched windows, black shutters, a big chimney; a wide driveway, a manicured lawn with foundation shrubs and a young tree, a back deck. Inside: a double-height foyer with a sweeping staircase and a chandelier; an open-plan kitchen with an island opening to a family room with a fireplace and big TV; a formal dining room; a home office; a mudroom off the garage; upstairs a primary suite with a walk-in closet and bathroom, three more bedrooms, a bonus room over the garage.
SIZE: about 44 wide (front, x), 32 deep, 14 tall to the top ridge, including the lawn and driveway; 1:1 scale, a player is 2 blocks tall.

